Zeno, Grand Livre, Nextesy and Pohoda; Stackurity (#6804) on security inventory beside VulX Watch; getwork.dev (#6805) on jobs data beside ATS Jobs, CareJobs.Now, Applystead and RobotTraining.jobs; Growth Radar (#6780) on the saturated visibility class; Shipbook (#6774) on observability; EZO Watcher (#6777) on monitoring beside Cronitor, Runheed and uptrack; Desktop Steward (#6773) on local files and agent infrastructure; EXTREMELY agency (#6781) on agent orchestration; OMX for Hyperliquid (#6775) and Solana Alpha x402 (#6803) on trading and agent payments; RoomLab (#6779) on media generation; Feedough Prompt Generator (#6778) as prompt tooling; Piratex (#6776) as a single-market creator vertical; DataXAPI (#6808) on scraping and social data beside LurkAPI and the Apify-actor hold. Core listings re-probed in the same pass: mcpservers.org still carries /servers/corpusiq-io in the canonical while the detail page answers 403, Glama answers 200 on /mcp/connectors/io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp with the CorpusIQ title and the 40+ description, the official registry carries io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote and a 30+ description that is now drift to correct at the next publish, Smithery could not be confirmed because the registry API errored twice and /servers/ returned 308 then 404 on redirect which is a routing change and never a delisting, and mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404 and the paid route declined. Counts: guide tree 1,102 directories before this pass and 1,103 after, 1,246 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,247 after.

Late morning sweep November 5 2026, one hour after the midday pass, and the two named surfaces answered in opposite ways. The mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap canonical came back set-identical to the 04:31 MST capture: 19,513 server URLs, zero additions and zero removals, the first exact empty diff this surface has produced after a week of namespace-prefix shuffles. Two counting notes go with it: the sitemap index now carries static.xml beside the twelve server and priority maps, so a raw union reads 28,851 URLs and 9,338 of them are marketing, topic and search pages, and only the /servers/ subset of 19,513 is the server universe; and /all returned 403 for the fourth consecutive pass, a standing condition rather than an incident. The mcp.so homepage carried the pass's whole delta and carried it only on the second read: the plain fetch returned 80 cards with the newest at 2026-11-05T06:47:30Z, the stamp the midday pass had already dispositioned, which reads as a flat feed, while a cache-busted read of the same page returned the same 80 cards plus one at 2026-11-05T17:29:38.960Z, so the plain read was 31 minutes stale and the two-read rule written for the three-hour ticks now applies at every interval. One server was catalogued. Konshus MCP - https://konshus.ai/api/mcp is remote stateless Streamable HTTP, registered as ai.konshus/memory 1.0.0 at 2026-11-05T17:35:03Z six minutes after the directory card, OAuth 2.1 with PKCE S256, authorization_code and refresh_token grants, a dynamic client registration endpoint and a single scope vault:rw. A keyless initialize returns 401 -32001 with the message that the server is stateless and every request must carry a bearer, and a probe token returns 401 Invalid or expired token, so the tier is documentation rather than a driven session. The eleven tools are read from the vendor's own table in four scope groups: summary get_whisper, get_briefing, get_persona_summary and get_vault_stats; recall search_atoms with as_of for a point-in-time view, search_artifacts over raw sources, recall_past_self, explain_what_you_know_about as a narrative with citations and whats_changed_since as a standup; capture log_signal, the only write and the reason the scope is read-write rather than read-only; and full mirror get_mega_briefing. It earns a guide on a gap rather than a neighbour, because the five memory entries here are agent working memory, Agentic Memory over Redis with FIFO handoff, AIS Memory with a W3C DID identity, MCP Long-Term Memory over Neo4j, Linksee local-first with a forgetting curve and SPM project-scoped with context packs, and none of them ingests a person's ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Grok history across 25 sources with 22 live, Google Calendar in beta and Apple Health plus Spotify announced, nor serves it back with a source and a confidence label on every distilled atom. Pricing is read off the pricing page as a five-tier ladder: Ember free with 50 memories and journal-or-paste ingestion only, Spark 49 dollars a year for 250 to 500 active memories and 10 GB over a one-year window, Founding 149 dollars a year for 2,500 to 10,000 memories and 50 GB over three years with all imports, Counsel 299 dollars a year for up to 35,000 memories and 100 GB over seven years, and Counsel Pro 599 dollars a year with a 300 GB vault and a lifetime window, against a founding cohort the vendor says has 1,456 of 4,000 memberships left. Limits recorded in the guide: a consumer product rather than a business data connector, vault:rw as the only scope so per-scope token issuance is the control that matters, encryption and discretion claims that cannot be checked from outside, self-reported usage figures printed on the vendor's own page at 99.81 percent seven-day uptime, 12,055 calls, 448 connected clients and a 0.9 second p50, and one vault per member with no team or per-client separation. Nothing else was held because nothing else arrived. Core listing check: mcpservers.org still carries /servers/corpusiq-io in