7 states and Washington DC, traces an LLC to the people behind it, returns a phone number and an email, and keeps the deal in the same workspace, with the agent drafting and the person sending so nothing leaves on the agent's authority and every change waits on a review link valid 15 minutes. 149 dollars a month, one plan, 7-day trial of 150 tokens with no card, 1,500 tokens a month for contacts and mail, 60 requests per minute per account, and no published tool inventory, recorded as a limit rather than filled in. It is not a duplicate of the real estate shelf, where Hercules, Dutch Property Context, AskRent and LucidRents run property management, DFX Intelligence and dfx-real-estate read parcels and recorded sales, and BatchData was held as a property and skip-tracing entry. Held from the rest with the class owner named: QuotedPart on manufacturing quoting, jobpostingsapi on jobs data, checkdomainrating on the twenty-guide SEO class, fanduelapi and PuntersEdge on consumer gambling, esimx on travel eSIM, agentscpa on affiliate operations, theopenapps on app store analytics, thenetworkery on DNS diagnostics, cgbb-org-ai-trust on trust and verification, mail-cuck and www-threadcamp-com on email, glpcompare-co-partners on the healthcare vertical with its keyless 200, three tools and check-date rule recorded for a later promotion, augur-trade on trading signals, the four pandadad0214 packs as one single-author fleet, bullpen as paid AI phone sales, cigo air care as a single-vendor industrial catalogue, heystacks on the document class, runlater, mobster and docs-strg as agent infrastructure, www-arca-inc-research as a Tokyo design agency, stayotter as travel, and the consumer and infrastructure remainder; quickbooks-bridge on accounting connectors, anymail-finder on email find and verify, and hunter-killer, ohmybug, smoover and fulfy-plus from the fresh mcp.so cards; MakeMidas on media generation, PuntersEdge on gambling, juris-licita-mcp as a regional legal and procurement vertical, Agentic Kingdoms as a consumer game, Fezola and GhosterMail on email from the queue. Six probes, one keyless 200, one protected-resource 200, four refusals. Core listing check measured: the canonical carries /servers/corpusiq-io and /servers/corpusiq/corpusiq-docs, the detail page answers 403 by edge policy rather than delisting, Glama answers 200 on the connector route, all four mcp.so slugs still 404, and smithery returned an error payload so no state is inferred. Guide tree 1,112 directories before and 1,113 after, 1,255 entries before and 1,256 after.

Evening sweep November 7 2026, fired on the 21:00 MST tick ten hours after the midday supplement, and the largest surface moved this time: the mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap universe went from 19,898 distinct server URLs at 11:00 to 20,000, from 63,359 raw loc entries across 12 server maps with 43,344 inline locale prefixes stripped. Against the 03:00 night capture that is 142 additions and 1 removal, and since the midday pass had already dispositioned 40 of them, 100 slugs were genuinely undispositioned in this window; two of the 142, DocPin and West Kite, were catalogued earlier today and only entered the sitemaps afterwards. mcpservers.org /all refused again, 403 direct and 401 through the reader proxy, the standing condition since November 4. The mcp.so homepage was read twice, plain and cache-busted, with identical results: 172 createdAt stamps, 129 cards, newest 2026-11-08T06:00:20.000Z, and 24 cards strictly above the 11:00 stamp of 2026-11-07T16:50:15.825Z, of which 19 carry consecutive stamps from 06:00:01Z to 06:00:20Z and read as one scheduled bulk publish two hours ahead of the pass clock, while five were ordinary arrivals (getcheapgames, pingstack, simplyboost, sell-my-data-to-ai, simvito-esim). The queue carried 19 numbers from 6902 to 6922 with 6905 and 6913 absent, all arrivals. Four servers were catalogued, and they line up on one idea without having been chosen for it. PointRover MCP at https://pointrover.com/mcp answered a keyless initialize 401 invalid_token naming its discovery document, and that document answered 200 with one scope read:tenant, so the tier is documented from the contract; nine read-only tools over a per-business board built in about an hour and checked every twelve hours, with pointrover_changes_since taking a board_version and pointrover_receipt returning the record behind a single figure, at 79 dollars a business a month after a 14-day trial. Patchwell MCP answered keyless 200 as Patchwell 1.30.0 with five tools, and the evide