Midday sweep November 8 2026, fired on the 10:00 MST tick seven hours after the night pass, and the canonical moved this time after two identical passes: the mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap universe went to 20,018 distinct server URLs from 63,435 raw loc entries across thirteen server maps, because a new servers/11.xml has joined servers/1 through servers/10, priority-servers and remote-mcp-servers in the index. Against the 04:01 capture that is 18 additions and 0 removals, and five of the eighteen were already prior dispositions, so thirteen slugs were genuinely undispositioned; twelve of those thirteen resolve to consumer verticals and six of them belong to one publisher. That is the structural finding of the window: vendawallet, carglendale, renderior, armenly, ayoh and kizupi are all io.github.miradero, six consumer verticals from one author, resolved through the official registry rather than guessed from domain-shaped slugs, and held as one fleet. mcpservers.org /all answered 403 direct and 401 through the reader proxy, the standing condition since November 4, so every new slug was resolved through registry.modelcontextprotocol.io instead, which answered for eleven of thirteen and turned a bare slug list into a product list. The mcp.so homepage was read twice, plain and cache-busted, with identical results: 204 createdAt occurrences, 188 distinct stamps, newest 2026-11-08T15:50:03.559Z, and exactly four cards strictly above the night stamp of 2026-11-08T08:56:02.072Z, all four held on classes this catalogue already owns. The submission queue carried eight numbers from 6936 to 6943 with no gaps, every one an arrival, and every one dispositioned by class. One server was catalogued. ListRiver MCP at package listriver-mcp 0.1.0 over stdio, registry record io.github.ListRiver-LLC/listriver active since 2026-11-03T13:24:59Z, answered a keyless initialize 200 as ListRiver 0.1.0 on protocol 2025-06-18 and returned all three tool schemas plus the server's own instruction set, with tools/call then returning the documented 401 naming LISTRIVER_API_KEY, so the whole surface is readable before a credential exists. Three tools, and the design decision is the finding: list_states and count_businesses are free and only search_businesses spends records, so an agent can size a market, narrow it on has_phone, has_email, naics, entity_type and formed_within for nothing, and retrieve names only once the number is worth it, with a cursor to continue rather than restart. The records are filings rather than profiles, address, county, registered agent and formation month plus phone, email, website, EIN and NAICS where the state publishes them, which makes a business filed last month a prospect with no website to audit and no ad history to bid against, a prospecting moment this catalogue could not previously reach for a US operator. Two limits came from the server itself and are recorded as the two ways it can mislead: phone, email, NAICS and county coverage is partial and state-dependent, with the server instructing the agent to check count_businesses before promising a phone list, and the records carry a use restriction barring credit, insurance, employment and housing decisions, which is the FCRA boundary stated plainly. Free tier 500 records a calendar month, then 50 dollars for 5,000 rising to 450 for 75,000, with prepaid packs and an AWS Marketplace path, and the record is the unit with every re-returned business counting again. Not a duplicate of corply-mcp, which is a formation service rather than a data source, nor leadbay-mcp and vibe-prospecting-mcp, which are proprietary scoring surfaces, nor firmy-ai-mcp, which reads one national registry and is silent on the US. Held with the class owner named: the miradero fleet as one publisher, picardo on the healthcare vertical class, rivieramayaelite on the regional consumer directory class, supercompress on the developer-infrastructure class, heimatvox-universalear on the transcript and document-workflow class, node driver and chromeleon on the anti-detect browser automation hold already recorded, and the staging-named agent-guard slug as a worker artifact rather than a product; from the feed seo-with-rankspot on the saturated SEO and AI-visibility class, whatsapp-by-green-api on the WhatsApp class, glp1-health on healthcare, and getsales on lead generation and sales engagement; from the queue dmswift, Kanvo, antiRea, Agent Index, Everstrike, Lodestar, Crossmart and PlayTesterHub. Core listing check measured rather than inherited: the fresh canonical carries /servers/corpusiq-io and /servers/corpusiq/corpusiq-docs, mcpservers.org /all answers 403 by edge policy rather than delisting, all four direct mcp.so slugs answer 404 so that listing remains absent, Glama answers 200 on the plural server route /mcp/servers/corpusiq-io while the /@benoit-p/ and /mcp/connectors/ forms answer 404 and the plural route is therefore the live one rather than a delisting, and Smithery returned zero servers on both q= spellings and a 404 on the direct page, which is a change from the previously verified unlisted=false state and is carried into the closeout as the one open question from this pass rather than recorded as a delisting on a single read. Counts: canonical 20,018 against 20,000 with 18 additions and 0 removals from 63,435 raw loc entries across thirteen maps, mcp.so 204 createdAt occurrences and 188 distinct stamps with four cards above the night stamp, eight queue numbers all arrivals, 30 candidates evaluated, one server catalogued and one guide, guide tree 1,120 directories before this pass and 1,121 after, 1,263 entries before and 1,264 after, 1,529 Markdown files under hermes/mcp/ before and 1,531 after.
Midday supplement November 8 2026, fired on the 11:00 MST tick one hour after the midday sweep, and both directory surfaces were quiet in the measurable sense. The mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap canonical returned 20,018 distinct server URLs from 63,435 raw loc entries across thirteen server maps, because servers/11.xml has been joined by nothing new and the index still carries servers/1 through servers/10, priority-servers and remote-mcp-servers, and the set came back identical to the 10:00 capture with zero additions and zero removals. That is the arithmetic proof that nothing arrived on this surface inside the hour rather than a stale read: the maps were fetched fresh and reconciled against the raw loc count before the diff was taken. mcpservers.org /all was not re-read and stays at the standing 403 since November 4. The mcp.so homepage was read twice, plain and cache-busted, with identical results: 188 createdAt occurrences, 115 distinct stamps, newest 2026-11-08T15:50:03.559Z, and zero cards strictly above the stamp the midday pass had already dispositioned, so the feed contributed nothing and the whole window is the submission queue. The queue carried two numbers, 6944 and 6945, both filed inside the hour at 17:24:41Z and 17:42:17Z, and both are arrivals rather than listing updates. Two servers were catalogued and each one is a first of its kind in this catalogue, for opposite reasons. Marsell MCP at https://getmarsell.com/mcp answered a keyless initialize 200 as marsell 1.0.0 on protocol 2025-06-18 and returned an instruction block that reads as an operating manual rather than a pitch, then listed all 126 tools with schemas and annotations, and a keyless tools/call returned the documented 401 naming the agent key, so the surface is fully documented and not driven. The finding is the direction of the delegation. Every other marketing entry here is a tool the assistant calls; Marsell is a client that calls the assistant back. homework_list queues the jobs the platform cannot do because they need the owner's own logins, files or inbox, and homework_done is verified by the platform itself for the jobs it can confirm, with a Google Ads job closed only once Marsell sees the connection. missions_next returns one message at a time, written and checked by the platform, to be sent word for word from the owner's own signed-in browser, and a refused mission is recorded rather than reworded, which is the honest answer to the platform-without-an-API problem. Facts and rules are separate stores: get_brand holds what the business is, owner_fact_set writes the owner's correction, and every plan, post and page reads it first. Money is quoted before it is spent, through picture_price, series_quote, business_read_quote and get_tokens, and the server instructs the assistant to say what a render costs before it runs. Setup is a scripted conversation that refuses to close until the owner's goal is recorded as one number and one date in their own words, and connecting the accounts and pressing Start are reserved to the owner by instruction, which is a consent boundary the entry records as a feature rather than a limitation. Plans run 49 dollars a month for 200,000 tokens to 799 for 3,600,000, annual at ten times monthly, extra tokens from 1.80 down to 1.50 per 10,000, with ad spend and creator fees separate from the token price. The class it enters is crowded and every owner is named in the guide: Toffu on ads, Maeve Social on publishing with scope gates, CampaignStack on outreach with approval budgets, Layers Growth on one TikTok loop, SocialBu and Omnisocials on publishing surfaces, and none of them dispatches work back to the user's own agent. Worth Leaving MCP at https://worthleaving.com/api/mcp is the opposite shape: one keyless tool, no account, per-IP rate limit, no inputs stored, registry record com.worthleaving/verdict 1.1.0 published 17:38:20Z, four minutes before the submission was filed. Its instructions string is two sentences and the second one is the entry: never compute vest dates or dollar totals yourself. Driven live with a two-grant scenario it returned take-it at 77 of 100, a walk-away cost of 62,500 dollars, an offer threshold of 230,000 dollars a year before tax, an annual net gain of 28,965 dollars and a next vest on 2027-02-01 worth 12,500 dollars, then sixteen numbered assumptions, two of which do real work: the leave date sent was in the past so the figures assumed leaving today, and with no ratings supplied the comparison is money only and the verdict says so. Three separable answers rather than one feeling, walkAwayCost, nextVest and offerHasToBeat, with verdict null when no offer is given, and share links that carry rounded bands rather than figures so a forwarded link does not publish the numbers. Limits recorded rather than discovered later: US metros only, engine closed, one document and one decision per call, and no portfolio view. Core listing check measured rather than inherited: the fresh canonical carries /servers/corpusiq-io and /servers/corpusiq/corpusiq-docs, /all is the standing 403 rather than a delisting, and all four direct mcp.so slugs answer 404 so that listing remains absent. Glama changed shape this hour: both /mcp/servers/corpusiq-io and /mcp/connectors/corpusiq-io now answer 301 to query pages on ?query=author%3Acorpusiq-io and ?query=namespace%3Acorpusiq-io, which answer 200 and report corpusiq-io matches, recorded as a routing change in the October 26 class rather than a delisting, with the card-level listing carried forward unverified on a single redirect. Counts: canonical 20,018 against 20,018 with zero additions and zero removals from 63,435 raw loc entries across thirteen maps, mcp.so 188 createdAt occurrences and 115 distinct stamps with zero cards above the previous stamp, two queue numbers both arrivals, two endpoints probed with both keyless 200 and one driven, two servers catalogued and two guides, guide tree 1,121 directories before this pass 